crosoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingShape" mc:Ignorable="w14 w15 w16se w16cid wp14"><w:comment w:id="1" w:author="Eiger, Ze'-ev D." w:date="2026-08-18T22:09:00Z" w:initials="EZeD"><w:p w14:paraId="55E911C6" w14:textId="47D528AD" w:rsidR="000D44D3" w:rsidRDefault="000D44D3"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/><w:rPr><w:color w:val="0000FF"/><w:u w:val="single"/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:bookmarkStart w:id="3" w:name="_cp_change_1"/><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/><w:color w:val="0000FF"/><w:u w:val="single" w:color="0000FF"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="0000FF"/><w:u w:val="single" w:color="0000FF"/></w:rPr><w:t>Add back since it is still mentioned later in the script.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:bookmarkEnd w:id="3"/></w:comment><w:comment w:id="4" w:author="Wang, Chenyi" w:date="2026-08-17T23:26:00Z" w:initials="CW"><w:p w14:paraId="6DFC2F38" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="007C0C5D" w:rsidRDefault="007C0C5D" w:rsidP="007C0C5D"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:t>Please update</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="5" w:author="Crocker Coulson" w:date="2026-08-14T11:58:00Z" w:initials="CC"><w:p w14:paraId="4502E83C" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00D757C3" w:rsidRDefault="00FC1B6A"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/></w:rPr><w:t>Square this 'timing / regulatory process' attribution with the 6-K. Note 16 now discloses CBP forced-labor detention notices (May 27-28) on Ethiopian cells, and finished goods built to $46.6M from $17.2M a year ago. A holder reading the 6-K may tie the shipment moderation to the detentions, not only the circumvention timeline. Counsel should clear the causal framing, and we should not overstate 'no change in demand.' A reactive CBP answer is in the Q&amp;A prep -- do not raise proactively.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="6" w:author="Crocker Coulson" w:date="2026-08-14T15:35:00Z" w:initials="CC"><w:p w14:paraId="1384F3C5" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0023321B" w:rsidRDefault="00FC1B6A"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/></w:rPr><w:t>HOLD per Rhone (Aug 14): do not finalize the AD/CVD / circumvention language — Rhone is preparing a separate consolidated response pending a factual and legal review of the wafer sourcing chronology, polysilicon sourcing, historical entries, VSUN activity and pre-initiation exposure. Keep the polysilicon claim period-bounded to current production. Separately, the 6-K (Note 16) discloses CBP forced-labor detentions and a finished-goods build to $46.6M; a reactive Q&amp;A is prepared — do not raise proactively.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="7" w:author="Eiger, Ze'-ev D." w:date="2026-08-18T00:27:00Z" w:initials="EZeD"><w:p w14:paraId="6B01ACD4" w14:textId="2824A030" w:rsidR="009459A2" w:rsidRDefault="009459A2"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:t>Earnings release says late 2027 or early 2028.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="9" w:author="Eiger, Ze'-ev D." w:date="2026-08-18T00:29:00Z" w:initials="EZeD"><w:p w14:paraId="70F6903A" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00A4793C" w:rsidRDefault="00A4793C"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/><w:rPr><w:strike/><w:color w:val="FF0000"/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:bookmarkStart w:id="10" w:name="_cp_change_5"/><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/><w:strike/><w:color w:val="FF0000"/><w:u w:color="FF0000"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:strike/><w:color w:val="FF0000"/><w:u w:color="FF0000"/></w:rPr><w:t>Not mentioned in earnings release.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:bookmarkEnd w:id="10"/></w:comment><w:comment w:id="12" w:author="Wang, Chenyi" w:date="2026-08-17T23:55:00Z" w:initials="CW"><w:p w14:paraId="295347C9" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00D124B3" w:rsidRDefault="00D124B3" w:rsidP="00D124B3"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:t>Not supported - consider deleting.  Operating expenses increased from $13.4m to $25.9m</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment></w:comments>